// The two-cases-per-function rule (docs/TESTS.md).
//
// A sibling of the action limit and the functions-per-file limit: a rule about
// the shape of a declaration, checked here rather than left to a suite. It is
// a *minimum* where the others are maxima, which is the whole point -- the
// other rules stop code from growing, this one stops it from arriving
// unverified.
//
// Off unless the build asks for it. Turning it on for a tree that has no cases
// rejects every function in it, so it is phased in per directory: see the
// rollout in docs/TESTS.md. `--require-tests` is what asks.
//
// `casefn` holds one entry per case, each the id of the function node the case
// was written under, so a function's case count is how many times its node
// appears there. The parser already builds it; nothing here re-parses.

check_cases() {
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import prog))) {
    check_cases_at(i);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return void;
given natcall_fixture ():() then calls check_cases_at:[1]
given case_fixture ():() then calls check_cases_at:[0]

// cases_short itself reads ut_at (../../report/host/why/note.id), which
// traps unless a case's `given` has also run ut_mark (report/host/mark/) --
// no fixture combines that with a real `prog` entry, so both cases below
// avoid ever calling it: case_fidx_fixture (back/tgt/c/emit/prog/test/judge/
// more/claim/more/hit/fixture.id) gives count_cases 2 hits (not short),
// natcall_fixture (back/ir/opt/run/pipe/cases/natfixture.id) gives a native
// row (exempt) -- the guard's two ways to skip.
check_cases_at(int i) {
  int n = count_cases((import prog)[i]);
  if(n < 2 && is_native((import prog)[i]) == 0) {
    cases_short(i, n);
  }
} return void;
given case_fidx_fixture (0):() then calls cases_short:[0]
given natcall_fixture (0):() then calls cases_short:[0]

count_cases(int node) {
  int i = 0;
  int n = 0;
  while(i < len((import casefn))) {
    n = n + case_hit(i, node);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return int n;
given case_fidx_fixture ((import fixture_fn)):(2)
given case_fidx_fixture2 ((import fixture_zero)):(1)
